  "subtitle": "Capture requested service, authenticated source, payer criteria, and supporting record; confirm decision and appeal.",
  "description": "Prior records requested service, authenticated source, payer criteria, supporting record, decision, and appeal. Prior evidence stays linked.",
  "use_case": "Use this prior authorization decision when staff must document requested service and authenticated source. Reconcile payer criteria, supporting record, decision, and appeal before the prior handoff. Use the service request, payer criterion, authenticated clinical source, supporting-document index, submission receipt, reference number, decision letter, and appeal calendar. This intake assembles a service request against payer criteria using authenticated clinical support, document indexing, submission prerequisites, reference creation, deadline tracking, and appeal readiness. Use a readiness inventory for prerequisite imaging, conservative-care history, benefit rule citations, attachments, missing-evidence requests, ordering-office ownership, and submission-channel preparation. Ask the assigned prior reviewer to confirm requested service against the organization's policy.",
  "risk_tier": "C",
